-- W2 scalar: || (CIf) combined with a negated comparison.
-- Was `!(3 == 3) || (4 > 2)` until #1739 half A repurposed `!` to Ref-deref.
-- There is no unary BOOLEAN operator any more — `not` is a prelude FUNCTION, and
-- the scalar path emits primitives only, so it cannot call one. The `||`-over-
-- comparison coverage this fixture exists for is kept via `/=`, which IS a scalar
-- primitive; a `not` spelling here would silently push the program off the scalar
-- path this fixture is meant to pin.
main = (3 /= 3) || (4 > 2)
